---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import aboutPhoto from '@assets/photos/about.jpg';
---

<section id="about" aria-labelledby="about-heading" class="section-padding relative">
  <!--
    No background, on purpose: the body is already --color-neutral-50. Hero's
    lower glow disc runs past the hero's bottom edge, and an opaque fill here
    painted over it and cut it along a straight line - a faint tangerine band
    ending exactly at the seam, most visible on a phone. Without a fill the
    glow fades out on its own blur. Don't "restore" bg-neutral-50 for
    consistency with the other sections.

    relative + content at z-10: the house pattern, see Hero/Services/Quote/Contact.
    A section left at position:static has its content painted in the in-flow
    phase, which the whole of every POSITIONED sibling paints on top of - so
    Hero's blur(120px) disc and Services' blur(64px) disc, neither of which is
    clipped on the block axis, were landing over this section's text. Being
    positioned puts this section in the same paint phase as the others, and
    z-10 on the content lifts it over any halo, which all sit at z-auto.
  -->
  <div class="container-prose relative z-10">
    <!--
      Five grid children, because the photo and the quote sit in different
      places at each breakpoint and one element cannot be in two places. On
      mobile the source order is the reading order: name, face, story, quote,
      CTA - the face arrives in the first scroll, and the quote comes after
      Gal has introduced herself. From lg the children are placed explicitly
      into two columns (column 1 is the right one, since grid columns follow
      dir="rtl"):

        rows:     1 auto | 2 1fr | 3 auto | 4 auto
        column 1: photo (rows 1-2, filling them), quote (rows 3-4, at the end)
        column 2: name (row 1), story (rows 2-3), CTA (row 4)

      The quote moved under the photo in Oct 2026 (Dan's call). In the text
      column it made that column ~730px tall beside a 496px photo, leaving
      ~117px of empty cream above and below the picture at 1440. Under the
      photo her words sit under her face.

      The two columns start and end on the same lines at every width, and the
      CTA stays 32px under the story. The quote is taller than the CTA, so it
      has to start higher than the CTA does: it spans rows 3-4 while the CTA
      takes row 4 alone, which makes row 3 exactly the difference between
      the two. Row 2 is 1fr, so the story, which spans rows 2-3, sizes it to
      whatever is left and row 3 is set by the quote alone (a spanning item
      that crosses a flexible track feeds only that track). The photo fills
      rows 1-2, so it ends where the quote begins, less the quote's own
      margin. Measured at 1024-1920: both edges level, 32px from story to
      CTA and from photo to quote. A fixed square photo could only match the
      text at one width (48px long at 1440, 173px short at 1024), and
      bottom-aligning the CTA instead pushed it 80-112px away from the text.

      Row gap is 0 from lg because the heading and the body are one continuous
      text block there; the body's own mt-5 is the spacing, and the quote and
      CTA carry lg:mt-8.

      No horizontal padding here: container-prose already insets by 1.5rem, and
      the text column used to add px-6 on top of that, which left this section's
      copy at 48px while every other section sits at 24px.
    -->
    <div
      class="grid gap-y-8 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-rows-[auto_1fr_auto_auto] lg:items-center lg:gap-x-20 lg:gap-y-0"
    >
      <!-- Name block: row 1 -->
      <div class="text-start lg:col-start-2 lg:row-start-1">
        <!-- Eyebrow -->
        <p class="eyebrow text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide text-teal-600">אודות</p>

        <!-- H2 -->
        <h2
          id="about-heading"
          class="font-heading mt-3 text-3xl leading-tight font-bold text-teal-700 md:text-4xl"
        >
          גל עופרי
        </h2>
        <p
          class="heading-rule heading-rule-start mt-2 text-sm font-medium tracking-wide text-teal-700"
        >
          פיזיותרפיסטית מוסמכת (B.P.T){' '}
          <span
            aria-hidden="true"
            class="mx-2 inline-block h-1 w-1 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal-500 align-middle"
          ></span>{' '}
          {
            /* The two credentials are one unit each: unbound, 360-390px stranded
              "מתעמלת" at the end of line 1, away from "תחרותית לשעבר". */
          }
          <span class="inline-block whitespace-nowrap">מתעמלת תחרותית לשעבר</span>
        </p>
      </div>

      <!--
        Photo: row 2 on mobile, the right column above the quote from lg.

        No height on purpose: the source is a tall portrait (104A8007 from the
        Oct 2026 shoot, pre-edit). Setting both width and height makes Astro's
        sharp service crop it at build time with fit: cover / position: centre,
        and the object-position below would then have nothing left to position.
        The framing is not a named build-time position, so the whole portrait
        ships and the browser does the crop. The box is square below lg, at
        45%: the window and its plants above her, the ball and the bed below.
        This is a wider frame than the 104A8009 close-up it replaced, chosen
        for showing the clinic around her; the cost is a smaller face and a
        sliver of the wall poster at the photo's right edge, which a portrait source
        cannot crop sideways. Re-check the 45% when the photographer's edit
        lands.

        From lg the box fills grid rows 1-2 (about 496x468 at 1440, 432x525
        at 1024; see the grid comment above), so the image is absolutely
        positioned: in flow, its natural 2:3 height would size the rows
        instead of the text. The min-height only guards against a story so
        short the photo would turn into a strip. The box is always less tall,
        relative to its width, than the 2:3 source, so the image still scales
        by width and the sizes attribute stays right.
      -->
      <figure
        class="shadow-card overflow-hidden rounded-2xl ring-1 ring-neutral-200/60 lg:relative lg:col-start-1 lg:row-span-2 lg:row-start-1 lg:min-h-[26rem] lg:self-stretch lg:rounded-3xl"
      >
        <Image
          src={aboutPhoto}
          alt="גל עופרי פיזיותרפיסטית מוסמכת יושבת על מיטת הטיפולים בקליניקה ומחייכת"
          width={480}
          widths={[400, 600, 800, 1100]}
          sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 496px, calc(100vw - 3rem)"
          loading="lazy"
          class="block aspect-square w-full object-cover object-[center_45%] lg:absolute lg:inset-0 lg:aspect-auto lg:h-full"
        />
      </figure>

      <!-- Story: row 3 on mobile, under the name from lg (rows 2-3) -->
      <div class="text-start lg:col-start-2 lg:row-span-2 lg:row-start-2">
        <!--
          Each sentence starts on its own line, like a personal letter (Oct
          2026, Dan's call). Breaks sit only at sentence ends, plus once after
          the greeting: a break mid-sentence would collide with the natural
          wrap on a phone and leave a stub line. Paragraph gaps still separate
          the three topics.
        -->

        <!-- Introduction -->
        <p class="mt-5 leading-[1.85] text-neutral-600">
          נעים מאוד, אני גל עופרי,<br />
          <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-800"
            >יש לי תשוקה אמיתית לעזור&nbsp;לאנשים</strong
          >{' '}
          לחזור לנוע בחופשיות ולהרגיש טוב בגוף שלהם.<br />
          הגעתי לתחום מתוך אהבה עמוקה לתנועה ולאנשים.
        </p>

        <!-- Personal story -->
        <p class="mt-5 leading-[1.85] text-neutral-600">
          כ<strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-800">מתעמלת תחרותית לשעבר</strong>{' '}
          שחוותה פציעות ותהליכי שיקום מורכבים בעצמה, אני מכירה מקרוב לא רק את האנטומיה, אלא גם את האתגר
          המנטלי הכרוך בכאב.<br />
          בשנים האחרונות אני מלווה ספורטאים, מתבגרים ומבוגרים בתהליכי שיקום ושיפור ביצועים.
        </p>

        <!-- Philosophy -->
        <p class="mt-5 leading-[1.85] text-neutral-600">
          מה שמניע אותי הוא הרגע שבו המטופלים מבינים שהם יכולים לחזור לרוץ, להתאמן, להרים את הילד
          בלי כאב, או פשוט לקום בבוקר ולהרגיש קל יותר בגוף.<br />
          אני מאמינה שטיפול הוא הסתכלות על{' '}
          <strong class="font-semibold text-neutral-800">האדם כולו</strong>: על ההרגלים, הנפש,
          והיכולת של הגוף לרפא את&nbsp;עצמו כשנותנים לו את הכלים והליווי הנכונים.
        </p>

        <!--
          No credentials list here on purpose (removed Oct 2026). Its badges
          only repeated what this section already says: B.P.T and the
          gymnastics background sit under the name, and "graduate of the
          physiotherapy department" is what B.P.T means. Bring one back only
          with qualifications the section does not already state (courses,
          certificates, licence number), confirmed by Gal.
        -->
      </div>

      <!--
        Quote: row 4 on mobile, under the photo from lg (rows 3-4).

        Gal's own sentence, approved by her in Oct 2026, wording revised with
        her in the same month. A pull quote rather than a heading: regular
        weight, a step up from body size, and an opening quotation mark in
        tangerine as its only ornament. The mark is a fill, like the site's
        discs and dots, so the text itself stays graphite. It was first marked
        with the .heading-rule bar, which made it read as a new heading, and
        before that with a coloured side border, a stock template tell.
        The glyph is Lucide's "quote" drawn filled: an ornament, not an icon.
      -->
      <blockquote
        class="mt-1 text-start lg:col-start-1 lg:row-span-2 lg:row-start-3 lg:mt-8 lg:self-end"
      >
        <svg
          aria-hidden="true"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="currentColor"
          class="mb-2 h-6 w-6 text-teal-400"
        >
          <path
            d="M16 3a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2 1 1 0 0 1 1 1v1a2 2 0 0 1-2 2 1 1 0 0 0-1 1v2a1 1 0 0 0 1 1 6 6 0 0 0 6-6V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2z"
          ></path>
          <path
            d="M5 3a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2 1 1 0 0 1 1 1v1a2 2 0 0 1-2 2 1 1 0 0 0-1 1v2a1 1 0 0 0 1 1 6 6 0 0 0 6-6V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2z"
          ></path>
        </svg>
        <p class="font-heading text-lg leading-relaxed font-normal text-teal-700 md:text-xl">
          המטרה שלי היא לא שתישארו אצלי לתמיד, אלא שתצאו עם ההבנה, הכלים והביטחון לנוע בחופשיות
          גם&nbsp;בלעדיי.
        </p>
      </blockquote>

      <!-- CTA: row 5 on mobile, under the story from lg (row 4) -->
      <div class="flex justify-start lg:col-start-2 lg:row-start-4 lg:mt-8 lg:self-start">
        <a
          href="#contact"
          class="btn-primary"
          aria-label="לתיאום ייעוץ ראשוני ופגישה ראשונה עם גל עופרי, פיזיותרפיסטית מוסמכת"
        >
          <svg
            class="h-5 w-5 shrink-0"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2" stroke-linejoin="round"></rect>
            <path stroke-linecap="round" d="M16 2v4M8 2v4M3 10h18"></path>
          </svg>
          לתיאום ייעוץ ראשוני
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
